{"type":"text","timestamp":1790410592065,"sessionID":"ses_f233b488effem9ADhEP66XcZCT","part":{"id":"prt_0dcc98f36001PlLprWwyG259YB","messageID":"msg_0dcc955ce001KiAatIajQGYhMe","sessionID":"ses_f233b488effem9ADhEP66XcZCT","type":"text","text":"Both files are implemented and the project launches cleanly in Godot 4.4.1 headless mode.\n\n**scenes/draggable.tscn**: Root `Area2D` named `Draggable` with `collision_mask=2`, `linear_damp=20`, script attached. Child `Sprite` (scale 0.58) with `star_1.png`, and `CollisionShape` with a 72×72 `RectangleShape2D`.\n\n**scripts/draggable.gd**: \n- `_ready()` stores `initial_position`/`initial_scale`, calls `play_spawn_animation()` (scale→0 then tween back)\n- `_input_event` detects `\"click\"` action to start dragging\n- `_process` lerps toward mouse at `20 * delta`\n- `_input` catches left button release → `_drop()`\n- `_drop()` emits `dropped(self, overlapping_areas)`, calls `self_destruct()` (shrink tween → `queue_free`) if not over `DropTarget`","time":{"start":1790410592054,"end":1790410592056},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_b67d5885-bbe4-4a89-9855-1084fb86e461"}}}}
